blocks.body:
Let $R = \bigoplus_{j\ge0}R_j$ be a finitely generated graded $k$-algebra with $R_0 = k$, $\mathfrak m = \bigoplus_{j>0}R_j$, and let $\theta_1,\dots,\theta_d$ be a homogeneous system of parameters: homogeneous elements of positive degree, $d = \dim R$, with $\dim_kR/(\theta)R<\infty$. Put $A = k[\theta_1,\dots,\theta_d]\subseteq R$. The following are equivalent:

1. $\theta_1,\dots,\theta_d$ is an $R$-regular sequence;
2. $R$ is a free $A$-module;
3. $R_{\mathfrak m}$ is a Cohen-Macaulay local ring.

If they hold, any homogeneous $b_1,\dots,b_r\in R$ whose images form a $k$-basis of $R/(\theta)R$ form an $A$-basis of $R$. (Hochster, section on Cohen-Macaulay rings in the graded and local cases; Wikipedia, graded version of miracle flatness.)

Let $(R,\mathfrak m)$ be a Cohen-Macaulay local ring and $x_1,\dots,x_n\in\mathfrak m$. The following are equivalent:

1. $x_1,\dots,x_n$ is $R$-regular;
2. $\operatorname{ht}(x_1,\dots,x_n) = n$;
3. $x_1,\dots,x_n$ is part of a system of parameters of $R$.

(Guan-Hu Theorem 4.13; Stacks Lemma 10.104.2.)

