Conventions to check before applying a result from a paper:
- depth relative to which ideal (usually $\mathfrak m$), and the value for the zero module;
- whether regular sequences require $M/(x)M\neq0$;
- whether "Cohen-Macaulay" for a non-local ring is tested at maximal ideals or all primes (equivalent) and whether $0$ counts;
- whether "maximal Cohen-Macaulay" allows $0$, non-finitely generated modules, or complexes;
- which dimension appears in $(S_n)$.

